Android port: lens profiles that can be loaded and chosen.

* The lens database (engine/src/lens_profiles.rs) is reloadable. Profile files (lensfun XML) loaded by the
  user are copied into `<settings>/lens-profiles` and read together with LIGHTCRAFT_LENSFUN_DIR.
* New commands (engine/src/cmd/lens.rs): `optics.lensProfiles` (list, filter, suggested and current),
  `optics.loadLensProfiles` and `optics.lensProfile` (choose a profile, "auto" or "none" for the active photo).
* `EmbeddedLens::profile_id` (develop/src/settings.rs) says which database profile a correction came from.
  A catalogue lens with a profile id wins over the lens the decoder found, and is part of the render key
  (engine/src/media.rs), so choosing a profile changes the render.
